s export/delete intents to services.\n58: \n59: ### Green\n60: - [ ] Add \"Export\" and \"Delete\" actions to the app controller.\n61: - [ ] Add export file chooser dialog.\n62: - [ ] Add delete confirmation dialog.\n63: - [ ] Make tests pass.\n64: \n65: ### Refactor\n66: - [ ] Commit: `feat(ui): Wire library export and delete actions`\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## Phase 5: Project Storage Layout\n71: \n72: ### Red\n73: - [ ] Write failing tests for project directory creation and paths.\n74: \n75: ### Green\n76: - [ ] Implement `internal/settings/paths.go` or similar.\n77: - [ ] Create `projectDir/recordings/` and `projectDir/verbal.db` on first run.\n78: - [ ] Make tests pass.\n79: \n80: ### Refactor\n81: - [ ] Commit: `feat(settings): Add project directory layout`\n82: \n83: ---\n84: \n85: ## Phase 6: Final Verification\n86: \n87: - [ ] Run `make check`.\n88: - [ ] Manual verification: import/record files, view library, export a file, delete a file.\n89: - [ ] Update `measure/tech-debt.md` and `measure/lessons-learned.md` if needed.\n90: - [ ] Update this `plan.md` and `measure/tracks.md`.\n91: - [ ] Commit: `measure(plan): Mark MVP library & export complete`\n\n(End of file - total 91 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Plan: MVP Library & Export\n\n**Status:** PLANNED  \n**Created:** 2026-06-12  \n**Focus:** Implement the library list view and basic export of the original media file.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Library Repository\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests for listing, deleting, and updating recordings.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Implement methods in `internal/db/recording_repository.go`.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(db): Extend recording repository for library operations`\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/plan.md","text":"# Plan: MVP Library & Export\n\n**Status:** PLANNED  \n**Created:** 2026-06-12  \n**Focus:** Implement the library list view and basic export of the original media file.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Library Repository\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests for listing, deleting, and updating recordings.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Implement methods in `internal/db/recording_repository.go`.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(db): Extend recording repository for library operations`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Library View Widget\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests for `ui.LibraryView`: renders list, emits selection and delete events.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Implement `internal/ui/library_view.go`.\n- [ ] Use GTK `ListView` or `ColumnView`.\n- [ ] Display title, duration, date, status badge.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(ui): Add library view widget`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Original Export\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests for `media.Exporter`: copies source file to destination with progress.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Implement `internal/media/exporter.go`.\n- [ ] Use buffered copy with progress callback.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(media): Add original file exporter`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: UI Wiring\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests that controller routes export/delete intents to services.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Add \"Export\" and \"Delete\" actions to the app controller.\n- [ ] Add export file chooser dialog.\n- [ ] Add delete confirmation dialog.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(ui): Wire library export and delete actions`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Project Storage Layout\n\n### Red\n- [ ] Write failing tests for project directory creation and paths.\n\n### Green\n- [ ] Implement `internal/settings/paths.go` or similar.\n- [ ] Create `projectDir/recordings/` and `projectDir/verbal.db` on first run.\n- [ ] Make tests pass.\n\n### Refactor\n- [ ] Commit: `feat(settings): Add project directory layout`\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Final Verification\n\n- [ ] Run `make check`.\n- [ ] Manual verification: import/record files, view library, export a file, delete a file.\n- [ ] Update `measure/tech-debt.md` and `measure/lessons-learned.md` if needed.\n- [ ] Update this `plan.md` and `measure/tracks.md`.\n- [ ] Commit: `measure(plan): Mark MVP library & export complete`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":91,"totalLines":91,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/plan.md","time":{"start":1781303654339,"end":1781303654738}},"id":"prt_ebdf8b3f3001HlKv1fyhXqc5Rm","sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","messageID":"msg_ebdf89202001JgXWX663OCS6Cn"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1781303655315,"sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","part":{"id":"prt_ebdf8abb0001x5Bhv8TJYkw6VJ","messageID":"msg_ebdf89202001JgXWX663OCS6Cn","sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","type":"text","text":"No graph.db. Let me check tech stack to confirm if TS, then read measure docs and track files.","time":{"start":1781303651248,"end":1781303655249}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781303655567,"sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_bdrk_01EKDqb1qop67z4gbDGdRFrF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tech-stack.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tech-stack.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Technology Stack: Verbal\n2: \n3: This stack is deliberate. Any change must be documented here before implementation.\n4: \n5: ## Core Architecture\n6: \n7: - **Language:** Go 1.24+\n8: - **UI Framework:** GTK4 + Libadwaita via `github.com/diamondburned/gotk4` and `gotk4-adwaita`\n9: - **Media Engine:** GStreamer via `github.com/go-gst/go-gst` (or `gotk4-gstreamer` if re-evaluated)\n10: - **Database:** SQLite via `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure Go, no CGO)\n11: - **Platform:** Native Linux (GNOME/Ubuntu focus; Wayland primary, X11 compatible)\n12: \n13: ## UI Layer\n14: \n15: - **Application Window:** Libadwaita `ApplicationWindow` with split-pane layout.\n16: - **Library View:** GTK `ListView` or `ColumnView` for recordings.\n17: - **Playback View:** Embedded GStreamer video sink (`gtk4paintablesink` preferred, fallback to placeholder).\n18: - **Transcript View:** Custom GTK widget displaying selectable word labels. No rich-text editor for MVP.\n19: - **Dialogs:** Libadwaita dialogs for settings, export, errors, and onboarding.\n20: \n21: ## Backend & Media Processing\n22: \n23: - **Recording:** GStreamer pipeline (`v4l2src` + `autoaudiosrc` or `pipewiresrc`/`pulsesrc`) muxed to MP4/MKV.\n24: - **Playback:** GStreamer `playbin3` or custom decodebin pipeline with frame-accurate seeking.\n25: - **Audio Extraction:** GStreamer pipeline to extract mono 16kHz PCM for transcription.\n26: - **Export:** GStreamer pipeline for stream-copy when codecs match, re-encode fallback otherwise. Single-segment trim for MVP; multi-segment concat post-MVP.\n27: - **Codec Detection:** Probe source file with GStreamer `discoverer` or a decodebin pad probe to decide stream-copy vs. re-encode.\n28: \n29: ## AI Integration Layer\n30: \n31: - **Provider Interface:** `internal/ai` defines the transcription contract. No OpenAI/Google SDK imports outside this package.\n32: - **Providers (MVP):**\n33:   - OpenAI Whisper API via HTTP\n34:   - Google Speech-to-Text API via HTTP\n35: - **Providers (Roadmap):**\n36:   - Local whisper.cpp via `whisper-cli` subprocess\n37:   - Real-time streaming provider for live captions\n38: \n39: ## Data Model\n40: \n41: - **Recording:** ID, title, media file path, duration, created_at, updated_at, transcription status.\n42: - **Transcript:** Recording ID, language, JSON blob of timed words.\n43: - **Word:** Text, start time, end time, confidence (optional).\n44: - **Segment:** A time range derived from selected words for export.\n45: \n46: ## Concurrency & Threading\n47: \n48: - All GTK UI updates from goroutines must use `glib.IdleAdd`.\n49: - Long-running work (transcription, export, audio extraction) runs in dedicated goroutines.\n50: - Use context cancellation for clean shutdown.\n51: \n52: ## Testing\n53: \n54: - Unit tests with `go test ./...`.\n55: - Mock external HTTP providers and GStreamer pipeline runners for headless tests.\n56: - Skip tests that require a display or hardware with `t.Skip` and a clear reason.\n57: - Target >80% coverage for core packages (`internal/domain`, `internal/ai`, `internal/transcription`, `internal/media/pipeline`, `internal/app`).\n58: \n59: ## Build & CI\n60: \n61: - Use `make check` for CI validation: `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`.\n62: - Export `GOCACHE=~/.cache/go-build` for faster incremental builds.\n63: - First cold build may take several minutes due to CGO/GTK bindings.\n\n(End of file - total 63 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Technology Stack: Verbal\n\nThis stack is deliberate. Any change must be documented here before implementation.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\n- **Language:** Go 1.24+\n- **UI Framework:** GTK4 + Libadwaita via `github.com/diamondburned/gotk4` and `gotk4-adwaita`\n- **Media Engine:** GStreamer via `github.com/go-gst/go-gst` (or `gotk4-gstreamer` if re-evaluated)\n- **Database:** SQLite via `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure Go, no CGO)\n- **Platform:** Native Linux (GNOME/Ubuntu focus; Wayland primary, X11 compatible)\n\n## UI Layer\n\n- **Application Window:** Libadwaita `ApplicationWindow` with split-pane layout.\n- **Library View:** GTK `ListView` or `ColumnView` for recordings.\n- **Playback View:** Embedded GStreamer video sink (`gtk4paintablesink` preferred, fallback to placeholder).\n- **Transcript View:** Custom GTK widget displaying selectable word labels. No rich-text editor for MVP.\n- **Dialogs:** Libadwaita dialogs for settings, export, errors, and onboarding.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tech-stack.md","text":"# Technology Stack: Verbal\n\nThis stack is deliberate. Any change must be documented here before implementation.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\n- **Language:** Go 1.24+\n- **UI Framework:** GTK4 + Libadwaita via `github.com/diamondburned/gotk4` and `gotk4-adwaita`\n- **Media Engine:** GStreamer via `github.com/go-gst/go-gst` (or `gotk4-gstreamer` if re-evaluated)\n- **Database:** SQLite via `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure Go, no CGO)\n- **Platform:** Native Linux (GNOME/Ubuntu focus; Wayland primary, X11 compatible)\n\n## UI Layer\n\n- **Application Window:** Libadwaita `ApplicationWindow` with split-pane layout.\n- **Library View:** GTK `ListView` or `ColumnView` for recordings.\n- **Playback View:** Embedded GStreamer video sink (`gtk4paintablesink` preferred, fallback to placeholder).\n- **Transcript View:** Custom GTK widget displaying selectable word labels. No rich-text editor for MVP.\n- **Dialogs:** Libadwaita dialogs for settings, export, errors, and onboarding.\n\n## Backend & Media Processing\n\n- **Recording:** GStreamer pipeline (`v4l2src` + `autoaudiosrc` or `pipewiresrc`/`pulsesrc`) muxed to MP4/MKV.\n- **Playback:** GStreamer `playbin3` or custom decodebin pipeline with frame-accurate seeking.\n- **Audio Extraction:** GStreamer pipeline to extract mono 16kHz PCM for transcription.\n- **Export:** GStreamer pipeline for stream-copy when codecs match, re-encode fallback otherwise. Single-segment trim for MVP; multi-segment concat post-MVP.\n- **Codec Detection:** Probe source file with GStreamer `discoverer` or a decodebin pad probe to decide stream-copy vs. re-encode.\n\n## AI Integration Layer\n\n- **Provider Interface:** `internal/ai` defines the transcription contract. No OpenAI/Google SDK imports outside this package.\n- **Providers (MVP):**\n  - OpenAI Whisper API via HTTP\n  - Google Speech-to-Text API via HTTP\n- **Providers (Roadmap):**\n  - Local whisper.cpp via `whisper-cli` subprocess\n  - Real-time streaming provider for live captions\n\n## Data Model\n\n- **Recording:** ID, title, media file path, duration, created_at, updated_at, transcription status.\n- **Transcript:** Recording ID, language, JSON blob of timed words.\n- **Word:** Text, start time, end time, confidence (optional).\n- **Segment:** A time range derived from selected words for export.\n\n## Concurrency & Threading\n\n- All GTK UI updates from goroutines must use `glib.IdleAdd`.\n- Long-running work (transcription, export, audio extraction) runs in dedicated goroutines.\n- Use context cancellation for clean shutdown.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit tests with `go test ./...`.\n- Mock external HTTP providers and GStreamer pipeline runners for headless tests.\n- Skip tests that require a display or hardware with `t.Skip` and a clear reason.\n- Target >80% coverage for core packages (`internal/domain`, `internal/ai`, `internal/transcription`, `internal/media/pipeline`, `internal/app`).\n\n## Build & CI\n\n- Use `make check` for CI validation: `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`.\n- Export `GOCACHE=~/.cache/go-build` for faster incremental builds.\n- First cold build may take several minutes due to CGO/GTK bindings.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":63,"totalLines":63,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/tech-stack.md","time":{"start":1781303655216,"end":1781303655457}},"id":"prt_ebdf8badf001WdNhi40MJRwPsq","sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","messageID":"msg_ebdf89202001JgXWX663OCS6Cn"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781303655569,"sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_bdrk_016DLUm8657Hnqh89XzCzjZD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Specification: MVP Library & Export\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: This track implements the recording library view and basic export of the original media file.\n6: \n7: ## Goals\n8: \n9: 1. List recordings in a library view.\n10: 2. Show title, duration, creation date, and transcription status.\n11: 3. Allow deleting a recording.\n12: 4. Export the original media file unchanged.\n13: \n14: ## Non-Goals\n15: \n16: - Thumbnails (post-MVP).\n17: - Search/filter (post-MVP).\n18: - Edited export with cuts (handled in the Text-Driven Delete track).\n19: \n20: ## Functional Requirements\n21: \n22: ### FR1: Library View\n23: - `internal/ui` provides a `LibraryView` widget.\n24: - Lists recordings from SQLite via the app controller.\n25: - Selecting a recording opens it in the playback view.\n26: - Delete button removes the recording entry and optionally the media file.\n27: \n28: ### FR2: Recording Metadata\n29: - Title defaults to timestamp; user can edit it later (optional for MVP).\n30: - Duration is stored in milliseconds.\n31: - Status badge reflects `New`, `Transcribing`, `Transcribed`, or `Error`.\n32: \n33: ### FR3: Export Original\n34: - \"Export\" action copies the original media file to a user-selected path.\n35: - Progress is reported via a simple callback.\n36: - Errors are surfaced in a dialog.\n37: \n38: ### FR4: Project Storage\n39: - Project directory structure is created on first run.\n40: - Media files live under `projectDir/recordings/`.\n41: - Database lives at `projectDir/verbal.db`.\n42: \n43: ## Acceptance Criteria\n44: \n45: - [ ] Library view renders recordings from a mocked repository.\n46: - [ ] Delete removes the recording from the repository.\n47: - [ ] Export copies the source file to the chosen destination.\n48: - [ ] Progress and error states are handled.\n49: - [ ] `make check` passes.\n\n(End of file - total 49 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Specification: MVP Library & Export\n\n## Overview\n\nThis track implements the recording library view and basic export of the original media file.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. List recordings in a library view.\n2. Show title, duration, creation date, and transcription status.\n3. Allow deleting a recording.\n4. Export the original media file unchanged.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Thumbnails (post-MVP).\n- Search/filter (post-MVP).\n- Edited export with cuts (handled in the Text-Driven Delete track).\n\n## Functional Requirements","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/spec.md","text":"# Specification: MVP Library & Export\n\n## Overview\n\nThis track implements the recording library view and basic export of the original media file.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. List recordings in a library view.\n2. Show title, duration, creation date, and transcription status.\n3. Allow deleting a recording.\n4. Export the original media file unchanged.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Thumbnails (post-MVP).\n- Search/filter (post-MVP).\n- Edited export with cuts (handled in the Text-Driven Delete track).\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR1: Library View\n- `internal/ui` provides a `LibraryView` widget.\n- Lists recordings from SQLite via the app controller.\n- Selecting a recording opens it in the playback view.\n- Delete button removes the recording entry and optionally the media file.\n\n### FR2: Recording Metadata\n- Title defaults to timestamp; user can edit it later (optional for MVP).\n- Duration is stored in milliseconds.\n- Status badge reflects `New`, `Transcribing`, `Transcribed`, or `Error`.\n\n### FR3: Export Original\n- \"Export\" action copies the original media file to a user-selected path.\n- Progress is reported via a simple callback.\n- Errors are surfaced in a dialog.\n\n### FR4: Project Storage\n- Project directory structure is created on first run.\n- Media files live under `projectDir/recordings/`.\n- Database lives at `projectDir/verbal.db`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Library view renders recordings from a mocked repository.\n- [ ] Delete removes the recording from the repository.\n- [ ] Export copies the source file to the chosen destination.\n- [ ] Progress and error states are handled.\n- [ ] `make check` passes.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":49,"totalLines":49,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/tracks/mvp_library_export_20260612/spec.md","time":{"start":1781303655101,"end":1781303655479}},"id":"prt_ebdf8ba61001LYVpJL95lLtL3v","sessionID":"ses_142079613ffeCsq2eayHwHhbpm","messageID":"msg_ebdf89202001JgXWX663OCS6Cn"}}
